### VPC Peering
- Allow link VPCs directly together
- We can connect VPCs within same AWS account or diffrent AWS accounts
- We can establish relationship between VPCs within or between AWS regions
- each VPC can have more than one VPC peerings
- AWS Cloud technician needs to allow the peering request from initiator
- With VPC peering in place, two resources in different VPCs can talk to each other using their respective Private IP addresses
- Peering connections are not transitive means if VPC1 peering to VPC2 and VPC2 peering to VPC3, VPC1 can't communicate with VPC3 directly.
- Flow
  - Create VPCs and Subnets
  - Create peering configuration
  - Accept peering request
  - Adjust route tables for both VPCs with CIDR of other VPCs
- two VPCs in VPC peering should not have overlapping CIDR range
- If Network ACLs or Security groups on VPCs block communication across VPCs, adding VPC peering does not establish connection unless Network ACL and security group restrictions are relaxed

